# EAS Build packs the repository ROOT when EAS_NO_VCS=1 (the phone build runs from app/, but the archive starts here).
# Everything the iOS build does not need stays out: the Rust workspace and its multi-GB target/, the Python
# services, the data tools, the infra. Found 2026-10-29: the copy of rust/target filled the disk and the upload failed
# with ENOSPC. With this file present EAS ignores .gitignore, so the usual ignores are repeated below.
rust/
api/
api-dev/
creative/
engine/
worker/
db/
infer/
gsync/
tools/
infra/
docs/
.github/
*.py
# the usual
.git/
**/node_modules/
**/.expo/
**/.expo-shared/
**/ios/build/
**/android/build/
**/android/.gradle/
**/dist/
**/web-build/
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log
**/__pycache__/
**/.pytest_cache/
